@identity.sigil from Identity import { user, actor }
@slotted.sigil from Slotted import { app layer }
@booking.sigil from Booking import {
  booking request,
  no-overlap rule,
  archive workflow,
}

component Rooms {
  goal {
    Let a user list a *room* that other users can request time on.
  }

  interface {
    An actor can create a room with *room metadata*, meaning a name,
    description, capacity and location text, and with a required *room timezone*
    that is not part of room metadata.

    Editing room metadata never changes the room timezone.

    The actor who creates a room becomes its *room owner*, and Rooms provides
    the room owner of each room. Only the room owner can edit its room metadata.

    Any actor can list every room that is not an *archived room* and open any
    room by its identifier.

    Rooms provides the *room lock*, a transaction that serializes every change
    affecting one room and gives the caller that transaction.
  }

  state {
    A room is active or an archived room, and Rooms owns the archived room
    mark.

    The room timezone is an IANA zone name.

    Capacity in the room metadata is informational; no request carries a party
    size.
  }

  logic {
    The room lock begins a transaction, locks the room row, runs the caller's
    work with that transaction, and commits or rolls back.

    Creating a room validates the room timezone against the IANA zone list and
    records the actor as room owner.
  }

  constraints {
    Only the room owner may archive, unarchive or change the room timezone.

    Rooms must not let the app layer invoke archive, unarchive or room timezone
    change directly; only Booking may invoke them, inside the room lock.

    Every change to a room's booking request records, availability, archive state
    or
    room timezone must run inside that room's room lock.
  }

  decisions {
    The room lock was chosen so automatic declines and approval re-checks see a
    stable room; the database no-overlap rule stays the backstop.

    Archive and room timezone change are reachable only through Booking because
    each needs a check or sweep over the room's booking request records; unarchive
    is part of
    Booking's archive workflow.
  }

  cases {
    Two changes to the same room arrive together; the room lock runs one after
    the other.

    Changes to two different rooms do not wait for each other's room lock.

    A room owner unarchives an archived room; it returns to the room list.
  }
}
